\paragraph{Consistency for structured IE.}
\citet{yao2026consistency} demonstrate task-level correlation ($\rho$ up to 0.47) between consistency and quality across NER/RE tasks; we diagnose why this correlation fails to yield selection gain, identifying entity-level failure mechanisms absent from their task-level analysis and providing operational bypasses ($+0.32$--$1.40$\,pp).
\citet{xie2023zeroshot} propose entity voting for zero-shot NER and \citet{xie2024selfimproving} report positive SC under zero-shot prompting where diversity is high---contrasting with our fine-tuned setting where degeneracy inverts diversity.

tool_args.new_string:
\paragraph{Capability ceiling vs.\ diversity collapse.}\label{sec:yun_contrast}
\citet{yun2025price} identify \textit{diversity collapse} under constrained decoding for discrete answers (Table~\ref{tab:differentiation}).

\paragraph{What is new relative to concurrent work.}
We provide the first instance-level diagnostic cascade for structured prediction: \citet{yao2026consistency} report task-level correlations without diagnosing selection failure; \citet{chen2023twofailures} identify failure modes without quantitative boundary characterization; \citet{xie2023zeroshot} propose entity voting without LP weighting or boundary analysis; \citet{yun2025price} study discrete-answer diversity, not structured IE.

